    ['Stack', 'React, TypeScript, Supabase, Cloudflare Pages, Paynow, Fakturownia, MailerLite'],
  ],
  filmAlt: 'Recording of the film on the eskapizm.com homepage: an evening at the laptop, windows with flights, stays and ferries, 33 to-dos in Notes, then the line Leave the planning to us, a phone with a plan-ready notification and the bay on Phi Phi.',
  filmLines: ['7 evenings at the laptop', '33 to-dos, 0 done', '“Leave the planning to us.”', '“Your plan is ready”'],
  filmNote: '(the film is in Polish)',
  beforeH: 'Planning a trip means evenings after work, and one person who has to figure it all out.',
  before: [
    'According to Expedia Group data from 2023, planning a single trip means visiting an average of 141 pages of travel content, and Think with Google counts over 500 digital touchpoints along the way. On the eskapizm website the client gets the same math in their own units: “That’s about X evenings after work. And one person who’ll have to figure it all out.” The promise on the site reads: “What if someone planned your trip for you?”',
    'On the company side, the person who plans that trip is Justyna. There are two of us, with no developers on payroll and no investor, so to keep that promise we needed a system, not a website with a contact form. The client app “My plan” has been running since October 2025, ordering with payment since November 2025, and the tool Justyna builds the plan in since January 2026.',
  ],
  kaskadaAlt: 'A frame from the film: a desktop buried in windows, flights, stays, the ferry from Krabi to Koh Lanta, a text from Mom and a Notes list, Thailand: to sort out, 33 to-dos, 0 done.',
  kaskadaCap: 'Seven evenings on one desktop: flights, stays, ferries, a text from Mom, and a to-do list in Notes that climbs to 33 items without a single one checked off.',
  routeKicker: 'Along the client’s path: count, order, get the plan.',
  // After the recordings on the sample plan (KIERUNEK section 4) this becomes the COPY-EN.md line “We follow one sample plan (...)”.
  routeIntro: 'We follow the path every plan takes, from the client’s first click to the board the two of us work from.',
  routeLabel: 'Plan route · Thailand, January 25 to February 9, 2027',
  routeNav: 'Plan route',
  stops: [
    ['The client counts', 'evenings calculator'],
    ['The client orders', 'order, payment, invoice'],
    ['Justyna builds', 'AI Plan Builder'],
    ['The client gets it', '“My plan” on the phone'],
    ['We run it', 'one dashboard'],
  ],
  s1: {
    h: 'The client counts their own evenings first. Only then do they see a price.',
    p: ['The calculator “How many evenings will you spend planning?” asks 4 questions about the route and how detailed the plan should be, and 20 seconds later it gives the answer in evenings after work. The numbers underneath come from Expedia Group and Think with Google research. The calculator has had its own page and a section on the homepage since February 2026.'],
    forWho: 'For the client', forTxt: 'before they see the price list, they have a number of their own evenings in their head.',
    cap: 'The calculator on a phone: four questions and the result in evenings after work.',
    alt: 'The eskapizm calculator on a phone (in Polish): a 20 seconds, 4 questions badge, the heading How many evenings will you spend planning? and a Check button.',
  },
  s2: {
    h: 'From picking a package to the invoice filed in KSeF, without either of us touching it.',
    p: ['Three packages: Basic, Full and Concierge. The price depends on the length of the trip (up to 7 or 14 days) and the number of people (1-4 or 5-8), and it’s calculated on the server. Whatever amount the browser sends is ignored. The client pays through Paynow, by BLIK (Poland’s mobile payment system), card or bank transfer. Once the payment is in, an invoice is issued in Fakturownia, our invoicing app, named after the exact variant, for example “Full plan (up to 14 days, 1-4 people)”. Company details come in from the tax ID, and the invoice’s status in KSeF (Poland’s national e-invoicing system, where every invoice has to be filed) syncs on its own. Ordering and payment have been live since November 2025, KSeF since June 2026.'],
    forWho: 'For us', forTxt: 'the invoice and KSeF don’t wait for one of us to sit down at Fakturownia.',
    reg: ['Paynow: BLIK, card or bank transfer', 'Fakturownia: invoice on payment, company details from the tax ID', 'KSeF: invoice status syncs on its own'],
    cap: 'Ordering on a phone: package, trip length, number of people, payment.',
    alt: 'The eskapizm order form on desktop (in Polish): a Plan Full card at 1290 PLN, switches for plan, length and number of people, a code field.',
    altM: 'Ordering on a phone (in Polish): a Plan Full card at 1290 PLN, Basic and Full, 7 and 14 days, 1-4 and 5-8 people, and a bottom bar with 1290 PLN and a Pay button.',
  },
  s3: {
    h: 'Justyna talks to the agent, the agent builds the plan.',
    p: [
      'AI Plan Builder is an internal tool in the admin dashboard where Justyna puts together the plan for a specific client; clients never see it. She talks to the agent in Polish, in everyday language, because that’s how we designed it: for someone who plans trips, not someone who writes code. The agent has 70 tools: it adds a flight as one card with the outbound and return legs, moves groups of attractions between locations, and lays the budget out in a fixed layout with a summary and a row-by-row breakdown. A screenshot pasted into the chat works as a “make it like this” instruction, and a PDF or DOCX document goes into the plan 1:1.',
      'The hard rule of this tool: the AI never deletes or hides plan content without an explicit confirmation. A server-side function detects hidden tabs, deleted days and a loss of over 40% of a day’s content, then holds the save and asks. Every save gets an automatic backup. “Plan check” shows only what the client would see as broken: an empty tab, placeholder text, an empty category. Justyna can also add a note to any section by hand or hide a single field, say the price or the time.',
      'One builder session is pinned to one client and their plan, and publishing updates the same plan the client sees on their phone. Justyna opens it from the client’s profile with the “AI plan” button. When something breaks, a problem report from inside the tool collects the last chat message and the steps to reproduce on its own.',
    ],
    forWho: 'For Justyna', forTxt: 'the plan comes out of a conversation, and nothing in it disappears without her say-so.',
    cap: 'AI Plan Builder: a conversation with the agent and the plan that comes out of it.',
  },
  s4: {
    h: 'The client gets the plan on their phone, with nothing to install.',
    p: [
      'The plan opens in the browser after logging in to “My plan”. It has 9 sections, in Polish: Getting started, Day plan, Attractions, Stays, Restaurants, Transfers, Budget, Packing list, Weather. Inside there’s an AI chat about this specific trip, with a query limit and a monthly AI budget per client, so the cost stays under control. A plan can also live at its own address without a login, as a private one-pager sent as a link.',
      'On the new homepage the same plan is told by a narrator: a phone pinned to the screen, text flowing beside it in 8 chapters and 3 acts (Before departure, On the road, Budget), and the screens are screenshots of the real app from the sample Thailand plan for January 25 to February 9.',
    ],
    forWho: 'For the client', forTxt: 'instead of a PDF in an email, they have a plan they open from their phone and can ask questions about.',
    cap: 'The plan on a phone: 9 sections, from “Getting started” to “Weather”.',
    link: 'The narrator on the homepage walks through the same screens the client opens on their phone once they’ve paid.',
    alt: 'The narrator on the eskapizm homepage (in Polish): a phone on the Day plan chapter, a Day 4 card for January 28, Phuket to Koh Lanta, and the heading Every day has its plan.',
    altM: 'The narrator on a phone (in Polish): a Your route card, 16 days, Phuket Old Town, Koh Lanta, Koh Yao Yoi, Phuket villa.',
  },
  s5: {
    h: 'One board for two partners and a “Report a problem” button.',
    p: [
      'The company’s tasks live in ClickUp in three lists: shared, mine and Justyna’s. The dashboard in our app mirrors them on one board with a Team / Kacper / Justyna / All switch, a calendar and an “Ideas” lane outside the status columns. ClickUp stays the source of truth, and the browser never holds a ClickUp token. A task deleted in ClickUp disappears from the board too.',
      'Every page of the dashboard has a floating “Report a problem or an idea” button, and reports land in one list with a red dot in the menu. Justyna reports from the place she’s working in, and I get the report together with its context.',
      'Justyna also has write access to the same repository, on her own branch, and she added a couple’s travel plan to it herself, under their own address. When the website and a blog post disagreed about Vietnam, Justyna settled on “a minimum of 10 days” and that’s what it says everywhere now.',
    ],
    forWho: 'For us', forTxt: 'the same task shows up in ClickUp and in the dashboard where Justyna builds the plans.',
    cap: 'The task board: Team space, calendar, “Ideas” lane.',
    repo: 'One codebase for both of us · Justyna on her own branch · changes reach main through a pull request',
  },
  ph: 'Dashboard footage: in preparation',
  restH: 'Around the route: four country pages, a blog, a quiz and a honeymoon offer.',
  restP: 'The homepage works as one system too: the film, the narrator and the sections below share one style of headings and buttons, and the page closes on the same Phi Phi photo the film ends on.',
  stripLabel: 'The rest of the system, scrolls sideways',
  strip: [
    ['Thailand: regions, seasons, a sample plan', 'First screen of the Thailand page: monks in orange robes by a temple and a large Thailand heading (in Polish).'],
    ['Vietnam: 10 days minimum, Justyna’s call', 'First screen of the Vietnam page: a night market with red lanterns and a Vietnam heading (in Polish).'],
    ['The Philippines: content served to search bots too', 'First screen of the Philippines page: boats on a beach under palm trees and a Philippines heading (in Polish).'],
    ['Indonesia: four countries, one page layout', 'First screen of the Indonesia page: a jungle waterfall and an Indonesia heading (in Polish).'],
    ['Blog: 23 posts written in the dashboard', 'First screen of the blog: a beach with palm trees and the heading Find your own escapism (in Polish).'],
    ['Honeymoons: a link for wedding planners', 'First screen of the honeymoon page: a couple on a beach and the line Fly to Asia. We will plan your honeymoon (in Polish).'],
    ['Quiz: 8 questions, results before email', 'The eskapizm quiz (in Polish): the first question from Justyna and Kacper as a chat and four answers A-D.'],
  ],
  scale: ['4 countries', '2 languages', '23 blog posts', '9 plan sections', '70 agent tools'],
  liveH: 'What’s live today.',
  live: [
    'eskapizm.com runs in Polish and English, with four destination pages and a blog with 23 posts.',
    'The client orders, pays and gets the plan on their phone within 7 business days. The kickoff conversation is about 60 minutes.',
    'The invoice and its KSeF status follow the payment on their own.',
    'The blog and the destination pages are rendered for bots at the edge of the network, from data, on every request, and any address outside the route list gets a 404.',
    'Production builds itself after <code>git push</code>, and the server functions deploy from GitHub Actions behind a test gate.',
  ],
  quoteTodo: 'Justyna’s quote goes here after the conversation. In production the block stays hidden until the quote is approved.',
  endH: 'Is there something in your company that one person still puts together by hand?',
  endP: 'Describe it to me in 15 minutes. I’ll tell you what I’d build first and what it would change.',
  btn: 'Book a 15-minute call',
  contact: '/contact/?service=' + encodeURIComponent('Application or system') + '#ctForm',
  more: 'Application or system: how I work', moreHref: '/services/apps-and-systems/',
};

// Cytat Justyny pojawia się dopiero po jej akceptacji (docs/case-studies/OPINIE-ROZMOWA.md).
const quote: { text: string; name: string; role: string } | null = null;
const url = 'https://mioduszewsky.com' + (pl ? '/pl/realizacje/eskapizm/' : '/work/eskapizm/');
const ld = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    { '@type': 'Article', headline: T.h1, inLanguage: locale,
      about: pl ? 'System eskapizmu: strona, sprzedaż, narzędzie do planów, aplikacja klienta i panel, eskapizm.com' : 'The eskapizm system: website, sales, plan-building tool, client app and dashboard, eskapizm.com',
      author: { '@type': 'Person', name: 'Kacper Mioduszewski', url: 'https://mioduszewsky.com' + T.homeHref },
      image: 'https://mioduszewsky.com' + SHOTS.film1440.poster,
      mainEntityOfPage: url },
    { '@type': 'BreadcrumbList', itemListElement: [
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'mioduszewsky', item: 'https://mioduszewsky.com' + T.homeHref },
      { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'eskapizm', item: url } ] },
  ],
};
const num = (i: number) => String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0');
const stations = [T.s1, T.s2, T.s3, T.s4, T.s5];
---
<!-- Przed publikacją: robots „index, follow, max-image-preview:large” (jak u Igora), dopiero po zgodzie w rejestrze (npm run verify:zgody) i deployu hero-film. -->
<VariantLayout title={T.title} description={T.description} bg="#FAFAF9" fg="#1c1917" switcher={false} robots="noindex, nofollow" locale={locale} alternatePath={T.alt}>
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(ld)} />
  <div class="case">
    <a class="skip" href="#main">{T.skip}</a>
    <header class="nav">
      <a class="mark" href={T.homeHref} aria-label={T.home}>
        <video autoplay loop muted playsinline preload="metadata" aria-hidden="true" poster="/logo3d/logo-nav-poster.webp">
          <source src="/logo3d/logo-nav.mp4" type="video/mp4;codecs=hvc1" />
          <source src="/logo3d/logo-nav.webm" type="video/webm" />
        </video>
      </a>
      <SiteMenu locale={locale} alternatePath={T.alt} />
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <article>
        <!-- 3.1 Scena: film w kadrze, na ciemnym brązie z klatki „Zostaw nam planowanie”. -->
        <header class="stage">
          <div class="wrap">
            <p class="kicker">{T.kicker}</p>
            <h1 set:html={P(T.h1)} />
            <p class="lead" set:html={P(T.lead)} />
            <dl class="meta">
              {T.meta.map(([k, v]) => <div><dt>{k}</dt><dd>{v}</dd></div>)}
            </dl>
          </div>
          <figure class="wrap film">
            <div class="film-frame d-only">
              <video class="vid" loop muted playsinline preload="metadata" width={SHOTS.film1440.w} height={SHOTS.film1440.h} poster={SHOTS.film1440.poster} aria-label={T.filmAlt}>
                <source src={SHOTS.film1440.webm} type="video/webm" />
                <source src={SHOTS.film1440.mp4} type="video/mp4" />
              </video>
            </div>
            <div class="film-frame m-only">
              <video class="vid" loop muted playsinline preload="metadata" width={SHOTS.film390.w} height={SHOTS.film390.h} poster={SHOTS.film390.poster} aria-label={T.filmAlt}>
                <source src={SHOTS.film390.webm} type="video/webm" />
                <source src={SHOTS.film390.mp4} type="video/mp4" />
              </video>
            </div>
            <figcaption>
              <ol class="lines">{T.filmLines.map((l) => <li>{l}</li>)}</ol>
              {T.filmNote && <span class="note">{T.filmNote}</span>}
            </figcaption>
          </figure>
        </header>

        <!-- 3.2 Przed -->
        <section class="paper before">
          <div class="wrap">
            <h2 set:html={P(T.beforeH)} />
            <div class="txt cols">{T.before.map((p) => <p set:html={P(p)} />)}</div>
          </div>
          <figure class="wrap shot-wide">
            <picture>
              <source media="(max-width: 900px)" srcset={kaskadaM} width="390" height="844" />
              <Image src={SHOTS.kaskada1440} widths={[720, 1080, 1440]} sizes="(max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px" alt={T.kaskadaAlt} loading="lazy" />
            </picture>
            <figcaption set:html={P(T.kaskadaCap)} />
          </figure>
        </section>

        <!-- 3.3-3.8 Trasa planu: pasek przyklejony pod navem (desktop), pigułka na dole (telefon), pięć stacji. -->
        <section class="paper intro" aria-labelledby="route-k">
          <div class="wrap">
            <p class="sec-kicker" id="route-k">{T.routeKicker}</p>
            <p class="intro-p" set:html={P(T.routeIntro)} />
          </div>
        </section>
        <div class="route" data-route>
          <nav class="route-bar" aria-label={T.routeNav}>
            <div class="wrap bar-in">
              <p class="bar-label">{T.routeLabel}</p>
              <ol class="bar-stops">
                {T.stops.map(([name, sys], i) => (
                  <li><a href={`#stacja-${num(i)}`} data-stop={i}><span class="bn">{num(i)}</span> <span class="bname">{name}</span><span class="bsys">{sys}</span></a></li>
                ))}
              </ol>
            </div>
          </nav>

          {/* Stacja 01: kalkulator wieczorów (papier) */}
          <section class="station paper s1" id="stacja-01" data-station="0" aria-labelledby="s1-h">
            <div class="wrap st-grid">
              <figure class="phone-shot">
                <div class="phone"><Image src={SHOTS.kalkulator} widths={[390, 780]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 360px" alt={T.s1.alt} loading="lazy" /></div>
                <figcaption set:html={P(T.s1.cap)} />
              </figure>
              <div class="st-text">
                <p class="st-label"><span>{num(0)}</span> {T.stops[0][0]}</p>
                <h2 id="s1-h" set:html={P(T.s1.h)} />
                <div class="txt">{T.s1.p.map((p) => <p set:html={P(p)} />)}<p class="for"><strong>{T.s1.forWho}:</strong> <span set:html={P(T.s1.forTxt)} /></p></div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </section>

          {/* Stacja 02: zamówienie, płatność, faktura (papier) */}
          <section class="station paper s2" id="stacja-02" data-station="1" aria-labelledby="s2-h">
            <div class="wrap duo">
              <div class="st-text">
                <p class="st-label"><span>{num(1)}</span> {T.stops[1][0]}</p>
                <h2 id="s2-h" set:html={P(T.s2.h)} />
                <div class="txt">{T.s2.p.map((p) => <p set:html={P(p)} />)}<p class="for"><strong>{T.s2.forWho}:</strong> <span set:html={P(T.s2.forTxt)} /></p></div>
              </div>
              <ul class="reg">{T.s2.reg.map((r) => <li>{r}</li>)}</ul>
            </div>
            <figure class="wrap set">
              <div class="screen d-only"><Image src={SHOTS.zamowienie1440} widths={[960, 1440, 1920]} sizes="(max-width: 1320px) 84vw, 1100px" alt={T.s2.alt} loading="lazy" /></div>
              <picture class="set-phone">
                <source media="(max-width: 900px)" srcset={zamowienieM} sizes="100vw" width="780" height="1688" />
                <Image src={SHOTS.zamowienie390} widths={[390, 780]} sizes="240px" alt={T.s2.altM} loading="lazy" />
              </picture>
              <figcaption set:html={P(T.s2.cap)} />
            </figure>
          </section>

          {/* Stacja 03: AI Plan Builder (zieleń, pełna szerokość, tor Justyny) */}
          <section class="station green s3" id="stacja-03" data-station="2" aria-labelledby="s3-h">
            <div class="wrap">
              <p class="st-label"><span>{num(2)}</span> {T.stops[2][0]}</p>
              <h2 id="s3-h" set:html={P(T.s3.h)} />
            </div>
            <figure class="wrap browser-shot">
              <div class="browser">
                <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
                {PANEL.builder
                  ? <Image src={PANEL.builder} widths={[960, 1440]} sizes="(max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1320px" alt={T.s3.cap} loading="lazy" />
                  : <div class="ph ph-wide"><p>{T.ph}</p></div>}
              </div>
              <div class="m-only chat-shot">
                {PANEL.builderChat
                  ? <Image src={PANEL.builderChat} widths={[390, 780]} sizes="100vw" alt={T.s3.cap} loading="lazy" />
                  : <div class="ph ph-tall"><p>{T.ph}</p></div>}
              </div>
              <figcaption set:html={P(T.s3.cap)} />
            </figure>
            <div class="wrap txt cols2">
              {T.s3.p.map((p) => <p set:html={P(p)} />)}
              <p class="for"><strong>{T.s3.forWho}:</strong> <span set:html={P(T.s3.forTxt)} /></p>
            </div>
          </section>

          {/* Stacja 04: plan w telefonie (papier) */}
          <section class="station paper s4" id="stacja-04" data-station="3" aria-labelledby="s4-h">
            <div class="wrap">
              <p class="st-label"><span>{num(3)}</span> {T.stops[3][0]}</p>
              <h2 id="s4-h" set:html={P(T.s4.h)} />
              <div class="txt cols">{T.s4.p.map((p) => <p set:html={P(p)} />)}</div>
              <p class="txt for"><strong>{T.s4.forWho}:</strong> <span set:html={P(T.s4.forTxt)} /></p>
            </div>
            <div class="wrap pair">
              <figure class="phone-shot">
                <div class="phone">
                  {PANEL.mojPlan
                    ? <Image src={PANEL.mojPlan} widths={[390, 780]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 360px" alt={T.s4.cap} loading="lazy" />
                    : <div class="ph ph-phone"><p>{T.ph}</p></div>}
                </div>
                <figcaption set:html={P(T.s4.cap)} />
              </figure>
              <figure class="narrator">
                <p class="link-line" set:html={P(T.s4.link)} />
                <div class="screen d-only"><Image src={SHOTS.narrator1440} widths={[800, 1200]} sizes="(max-width: 1320px) 60vw, 760px" alt={T.s4.alt} loading="lazy" /></div>
                <div class="screen m-only"><Image src={SHOTS.narrator390} widths={[390]} sizes="100vw" alt={T.s4.altM} loading="lazy" /></div>
              </figure>
            </div>
          </section>

          {/* Stacja 05: jeden panel wspólników (zieleń) */}
          <section class="station green s5" id="stacja-05" data-station="4" aria-labelledby="s5-h">
            <div class="wrap">
              <p class="st-label"><span>{num(4)}</span> {T.stops[4][0]}</p>
              <h2 id="s5-h" set:html={P(T.s5.h)} />
              <div class="txt cols2">
                {T.s5.p.map((p) => <p set:html={P(p)} />)}
                <p class="for"><strong>{T.s5.forWho}:</strong> <span set:html={P(T.s5.forTxt)} /></p>
              </div>
            </div>
            <figure class="wrap panel">
              <div class="browser">
                <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
                {PANEL.tasks
                  ? <Image src={PANEL.tasks} widths={[960, 1440]} sizes="(max-width: 1320px) 100vw, 1100px" alt={T.s5.cap} loading="lazy" />
                  : <div class="ph ph-wide"><p>{T.ph}</p></div>}
              </div>
              <div class="browser small">
                <span class="dots" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
                {PANEL.issues
                  ? <Image src={PANEL.issues} widths={[720, 1440]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 520px" alt="" loading="lazy" />
                  : <div class="ph ph-wide"><p>{T.ph}</p></div>}
              </div>
              <figcaption set:html={P(T.s5.cap)} />
            </figure>
            <p class="wrap repo">{T.s5.repo}</p>
          </section>
        </div>
        <div class="route-pill" data-pill aria-hidden="true"><span class="pn">01</span> <span class="pt">{T.stops[0][0]}</span></div>

        <!-- 3.9 Reszta systemu w jednym pasie, przewijanym w poziomie -->
        <section class="paper rest" aria-labelledby="rest-h">
          <div class="wrap">
            <h2 id="rest-h" set:html={P(T.restH)} />
            <p class="txt" set:html={P(T.restP)} />
          </div>
          <div class="strip" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label={T.stripLabel} data-strip>
            <ul>
              {SHOTS.strip.map((src, i) => (
                <li>
                  <figure>
                    <Image src={src} widths={[640, 960, 1280]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 84vw, 576px" alt={T.strip[i][1]} loading="lazy" />
                    <figcaption>{T.strip[i][0]}</figcaption>
                  </figure>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
          <p class="wrap scale">{T.scale.map((s, i) => <>{i === 3 && <i class="br" aria-hidden="true"></i>}<span>{s}</span></>)}</p>
        </section>

        <!-- 3.10 Co działa dziś, cytat Justyny -->
        <section class="paper live-now" aria-labelledby="live-h">
          <div class="wrap duo">
            <h2 id="live-h">{T.liveH}</h2>
            <ul class="live-list">{T.live.map((l) => <li><span set:html={P(l)} /></li>)}</ul>
          </div>
        </section>

        {quote ? (
          <figure class="wrap quote">
            <blockquote><p>{quote.text}</p></blockquote>
            <figcaption>{quote.name}, {quote.role}</figcaption>
          </figure>
        ) : import.meta.env.DEV && (
          <aside class="wrap quote-todo" aria-hidden="true">{T.quoteTodo}</aside>
        )}
      </article>

      <section class="end" aria-labelledby="end-h">
        <div class="wrap end-in">
          <h2 id="end-h" set:html={P(T.endH)} />
          <div>
            <p set:html={P(T.endP)} />
            <a class="btn" href={T.contact}>{T.btn}</a>
            <p class="more"><a href={T.moreHref}>{T.more}</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>
    <BrandFooter locale={locale} inset />
  </div>
</VariantLayout>

<script>
  // Pętle filmu grają tylko w ekranie i bez prefers-reduced-motion; inaczej zostaje plakat.
  // Ukryta wersja (desktop albo telefon) nigdy nie przecina ekranu, więc się nie odtwarza.
  const still = matchMedia('(prefers-reduced-motion: reduce)');
  const io = new IntersectionObserver((es) => es.forEach((e) => {
    const v = e.target as HTMLVideoElement;
    if (e.isIntersecting && !still.matches) v.play().catch(() => {}); else v.pause();
  }), { threshold: .2 });
  const vids = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLVideoElement>('.case video.vid')];
  vids.forEach((v) => io.observe(v));
  // Zmiana ustawienia w trakcie: pauza od razu, a po wyłączeniu wznowienie przez ponowne obserwowanie.
  still.addEventListener('change', () => vids.forEach((v) => { v.pause(); io.unobserve(v); io.observe(v); }));

  // Pasek trasy: bieżąca stacja = ostatnia, której górna krawędź minęła 45% wysokości okna.
  const route = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-route]');
  const stations = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-station]')];
  const links = [...document.querySelectorAll<HTMLAnchorElement>('[data-stop]')];
  const pill = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-pill]');
  const names = links.map((a) => a.querySelector('.bname')?.textContent || '');
  let current = -2;
  let ticking = false;
  const update = () => {
    ticking = false;
    if (!route || !pill) return;
    const line = innerHeight * .45;
    let idx = -1;
    stations.forEach((s, i) => { if (s.getBoundingClientRect().top <= line) idx = i; });
    const r = route.getBoundingClientRect();
    pill.classList.toggle('on', idx >= 0 && r.bottom > line);
    if (idx === current) return;
    current = idx;
    const shown = Math.max(idx, 0);
    links.forEach((a, i) => { if (i === shown && idx >= 0) a.setAttribute('aria-current', 'step'); else a.removeAttribute('aria-current'); });
    route.dataset.current = idx >= 0 ? String(shown) : '';
    pill.querySelector('.pn')!.textContent = String(shown + 1).padStart(2, '0');
    pill.querySelector('.pt')!.textContent = names[shown];
  };
  const onScroll = () => { if (!ticking) { ticking = true; requestAnimationFrame(update); } };
  addEventListener('scroll', onScroll, { passive: true });
  addEventListener('resize', onScroll);
  update();

  // Pas „reszta systemu”: kółko myszy przewija pas w poziomie, dopóki ma dokąd; na końcach przewija się strona.
  const strip = document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-strip]');
  strip?.addEventListener('wheel', (e) => {
    if (Math.abs(e.deltaY) <= Math.abs(e.deltaX)) return;
    const max = strip.scrollWidth - strip.clientWidth;
    // deltaMode: 0 piksele, 1 linie, 2 strony.
    const dy = e.deltaY * (e.deltaMode === 1 ? 16 : e.deltaMode === 2 ? strip.clientWidth : 1);
    const next = strip.scrollLeft + dy;
    if ((e.deltaY < 0 && strip.scrollLeft <= 0) || (e.deltaY > 0 && strip.scrollLeft >= max - 1)) return;
    e.preventDefault();
    strip.scrollLeft = Math.max(0, Math.min(max, next));
  }, { passive: false });
</script>

